+
+## Checks completed in this packaging environment
+
+- Baseline file identity against GitHub V26: PASS for the critical server/client/test files using Git blob hashes.
+- `npm run verify:source`: PASS.
+- TypeScript/TSX syntax transpile across all 41 `.ts/.tsx` source files: PASS.
+- Tenant authorization and overlap core checks: PASS.
+- Customer session persistence and per-tenant isolation test with simulated localStorage/window: PASS.
+- Admin logout preserving customer cancellation capability (`booking_access__<tenant>`): PASS.
+- Secret scan for embedded Firebase private keys / non-empty Telnyx secrets: PASS.
+- Firestore transaction batching uses documented `Transaction.getAll(...)` while retaining the booking-day guard and same-day overlap read before writes.
+
+## Not executed here
+
+A full `npm ci`, Vite/esbuild production build and Firebase emulator integration suite could not run in this container because dependencies are not installed and external npm registry access is unavailable. The Render build remains configured to execute source verification, the production build and `verify-dist` automatically.
+
+## Deployment acceptance
+
+1. Deploy this package/repository state to Render.
+2. Confirm `/api/health` returns `version: 26.0.1`.
+3. Register a customer, refresh the page, and confirm the customer stays signed in.
+4. Switch between `alex_beauty` and `avi` and confirm the customer profile does not cross tenants.
+5. Book one appointment and confirm it appears once and blocks the slot.
+6. Cancel it and confirm the slot reopens.
+7. If booking still feels slow, inspect Render logs for `[Performance] slow booking ... duration=...ms`.
